      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with no new snow recorded overnight or in the last 24 hours and snow forecast to develop through the day. The mountain is currently 0°C, with winds of 16 km/h and gusts to 27 km/h. The resort says coverage remains superb, with groomers active overnight; groomed terrain will start firm and fast, while pockets of cold dry snow remain at higher, shaded elevations. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow’s Quad and Wells Pipe Platter are open. Learners Slopes, Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Little Willows, Big Willows, Ski Touring Access and Arcadia Chutes are open, while Mt Cardrona and Summit are on hold. Big Air is closed and Gravity Cross is an event area. (Issued: 11:03 am, 16 Sep) The access road has an active road hazard advisory and all vehicles must carry chains. The Schools Alpine Race is taking place in the cross course today, while the Platter and Olympic Pipe close at 11:45 am. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
