      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with no new snow recorded overnight, in the last 24 hours or over the last 7 days. The mountain is currently 1°C, with winds of 16 km/h and gusts to 31 km/h. The resort expects snow through the day as the freezing level falls, with the lower Home Basin offering spring conditions and better skiing higher up. Home Basin Express and Beginner Platter are open, while Saddle Quad is closed. Open terrain includes Home Basin, Lower Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin and Terrain Park; Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes, Motatapu Chutes, Backcountry Access and Skinning Access are closed. Open groomers include Triple Treat, Beginner Platter, Big Skite and Main Street. (Issued: 10:14 am, 16 Sep) The access road is subject to an active road hazard advisory, and all vehicles must carry chains because of the incoming snow. The resort is focusing operations on Home Basin, while Saddle Basin remains closed because of the incoming storm and avalanche concerns on Saddle Track. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 2 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
